{
	"_description": "HID usage of each physical key, by the key ids of physical_keys.json. Read only by the macOS key-identity codegen (tools/codegen/codegen-hid-key-identity-hs.cjs), which turns the raw usages of the physical-key stream into the macOS keycodes the metrics store; the other drivers never parse it, which is why it is not a column of the registry every driver loads. tools/test/test-physical-keys-registry.cjs validates it against the registry and the USB HID Usage Tables.",
	"_fields": {
		"aliases": "Optional, on a key: further {page, usage} a keyboard may send for the same position, such as Keyboard Non-US # (0x32), the PC ISO key left of Return that macOS and Linux report as Backslash.",
		"unregistered": "Keys real keyboards send that no layer can bind, so the registry has no position for them, by KeyboardEvent.code: {page, usage, hs}, hs being the macOS virtual keycode (kVK_*) macOS reports for that usage. A PC keyboard's PrintScreen, ScrollLock and Pause are F13, F14 and F15 on macOS.",
		"keys": "Registry key id -> {page, usage}: the USB HID usage of the key's position (page 7 Keyboard/Keypad, page 12 Consumer), the same on every OS and form. macOS reports the keys at usages 0x35 and 0x64 with swapped keycodes on an ISO keyboard (macos_iso in the registry), so a raw usage resolves to a keycode through the device's form."
	},
